Z||000000||Trixi||11-19-1999||10:45 AM||||I just bought a 84 4-speed standard, and had to replace the shifting cable.  Now that that has happened there is no reverse.  I think that the selector cable could be bad, but not sure. Could be alignment?  Help please!||||reg||9
Z||000001||Rodrv6||11-19-1999||11:21 AM||||Did reverse work before the shift cable was changed?  It probably is an adjustment problem.  The adjustment procedure in the service manual is a bit confusing to read, but it works if you follow it step by step.  I've never tried the procedure in the Haynes book, so I don't know how well it works.  There is a spring in the transaxle that has to be compressed in order to find reverse. If the select cable is out of adjustment it is nearly impossible to find reverse.||||reg||7
